  "title": "One band makes the torus",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "For equally spaced networks of rule-60 rings with law (12,12) contacts: (1) every n x m torus with n >= 3, m >= 2 (or n = 2, m >= 3) has a half-turn at every contact exchanging its rings, so every contact persists at every lag; (2) inserting one band into a loop of n >= 3 rings, each new ring joined to its partner by two contacts, one on each side, gives the n x 2 torus, and further bands give the n x m tori: from a loop, the band law makes the torus at its first step and keeps every contact persistent at every stage.",
